      "title": "Trinketry introduces preserved design elements as anchors for generative exploration",
      "summary": "Researchers introduced trinkets, user-preserved design elements that function as reusable materials, retrieval queries, and navigational anchors. The technique helps visual designers preserve promising ideas and context amid proliferating generated alternatives.",
      "design_implication": "A designer reviewing dozens of AI variants easily loses the exact visual fragment that worked in an earlier concept. When preserved sub-elements serve as direct queries and navigational anchors, exploration stops being disposable prompting and becomes an accretive, traceable history.",
